{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאמר יהודה הוציאוה ותשרף", :translit "va'yomer yehudah hotzi'uha ve'tisaref", :gloss "And Judah said, Bring her forth, and let her be burnt"} {:he "הוציאוה ותשרף", :translit "hotzi'uha ve'tisaref", :gloss "Bring her forth and let her be burnt"} {:he "שם בן ארבע", :translit "shem ben arba", :gloss "Shem son of four"} {:he "הסימנין", :translit "ha'simanin", :gloss "the signs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "הוציאוה ותשרף", :spells "הוי\"ב"}], :frame {:text "Tamar demanded pledges from Judah: his seal, cord, and staff (Genesis 38:18). When Judah ordered her execution, she produced these 'signs' to identify him as the father. The midrashic reading calls Shem 'son of four,' because his name שם equals 300 in gematria and four generations later appear, or more precisely the letters of שם בן ארבע correspond to the initial letters of הוציאוה ותשרף, signaling that God orchestrated events so Tamar would have the pledges at the decisive moment (Genesis Rabbah 85:11). Rashi on Genesis 38:25 calls the pledged items סימנין, 'signs,' by which Judah recognized his own.", :sources ["Genesis 38:18" "Genesis 38:25" "Genesis Rabbah 85:11" "Rashi on Genesis 38:25"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הוציאוה ותשרף", :translit "hotzi'uha ve'tisaref", :gloss "Bring her forth and let her be burnt"} {:he "בת כהן שזינתה בשריפה", :translit "bat kohen she'zinta bi'sreifah", :gloss "a daughter of a priest who commits harlotry by burning"} {:he "צדקה ממני", :translit "tzadkah mimeni", :gloss "She is more righteous than I"} {:he "אשר תזנה עליו", :translit "asher tizneh alav", :gloss "who commits harlotry against him"} {:he "אשר תזנה תחת אישה", :translit "asher tizneh tachat ishah", :gloss "who commits harlotry under her husband"} {:he "הוציאוה ותשרף", :translit "hotzi'uha ve'tisaref", :gloss "Bring her forth and let her be burnt"} {:he "הוציאוה ותשרף", :translit "hotzi'uha ve'tisaref", :gloss "Bring her forth and let her be burnt"} {:he "פנוי הבא על הפנויה", :translit "panui ha'ba al ha'pnuya", :gloss "an unmarried man who has relations with an unmarried woman"} {:he "בית דינו של שם", :translit "beit dino shel shem", :gloss "the court of Shem"} {:he "מעשה דתמר", :translit "ma'aseh d'tamar", :gloss "the incident of Tamar"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Survey of legal difficulties and multiple resolutions from Rashi, Ramban, R. Judah the Pious, and midrashic sources"} {:kind :other, :note "Cites Sanhedrin on levirate marriage not applying to children of Noah; cites Avodah Zarah on court of Shem"}], :frame {:text "Rashi on Genesis 38:24 identifies Tamar as the daughter of Shem, a priest, so her execution by fire follows the law of Leviticus 21:9. Ramban objects that Leviticus 21:9 applies only to a betrothed or married daughter of a priest; a yevama is only under a negative prohibition (yevamah lo le'shuk, based on Deuteronomy 25:5); levirate marriage does not apply to children of Noah (Sanhedrin 59a); and Noahide law prescribes only the sword (Sanhedrin 57a). He therefore explains that Judah acted by royal prerogative. R. Judah the Pious reads 'burning' as branding a mark, not execution. Sanhedrin 18a-b states a king neither judges nor is judged; Sanhedrin 32a states capital cases begin from the side; Sotah 7b and Sanhedrin 3a prohibit judging a relative. Genesis Rabbah 85:10 records that Shem judged Tamar, while Avodah Zarah 36b states the court of Shem decreed burning for an unmarried man with an unmarried woman.", :sources ["Rashi on Genesis 38:24" "Leviticus 21:9" "Deuteronomy 25:5" "Sanhedrin 59a" "Sanhedrin 57a" "Sanhedrin 18a-b" "Sanhedrin 32a" "Sotah 7b" "Sanhedrin 3a" "Genesis Rabbah 85:10" "Avodah Zarah 36b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "הוציאוה ותשרף", :spells "הוי\"ב", :letters ["ה" "ו"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :other, :note "Survey of legal difficulties and multiple resolutions from Rashi, Ramban, R. Judah the Pious, and midrashic sources", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Cites Sanhedrin on levirate marriage not applying to children of Noah; cites Avodah Zarah on court of Shem", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:55.309238437Z", :model "glm-5.2"}